      "summary": "Re-validated and refined /workspace/impl_diffs/datasets.md into apply-ready /workspace/impl_diffs/datasets_v2.md against the live grokking_race_v2.py (2505 lines). All OLD snippets copied verbatim; line numbers re-checked (no drift). Spec adds: (1) NEW grokking_optimizers/dataset_sources.py — a torch-only, no-download importable stub returning the legacy 6-tuple (fixed streaming train VIEW + fixed eval PROBE) for FineWeb-Edu/decoder, ImageNet-1k/vit, GiftEvalPretrain/mamba, deterministic by (seed,step,salt) for A/A/A; (2) Edit 2.1 DEFAULT_CONFIG DEFAULT-OFF knobs (data_source=modular + train_batch_size/train_view_rows/eval_probe_rows/eval_micro_batch/early_stop_mode=acc/plateau_patience/min_delta); (3) Edit 2.2 make_data_for_task dispatch (modular branch = literal original 4 lines, byte-identical; non-modular lazily imports the stub); (4) Edit 2.3 evaluate() inert-when-OFF fixed-probe-capped micro-batched forward (micro_batch<=0 → original single-shot); (5) Edit 2.4 EarlyStopper mode=acc default + loss-PLATEAU branch (acc tail = literal original); (6) Edits 2.5/2.6a/2.6b _stopper + _eval_log thread loss to stopper only in loss-mode; (7) Edits 2.7a/2.7b/2.8 capped final eval threaded via _fin function-attribute set in _tr (no signature widening) + plateau-aware confirm; (8) Edit 2.9 remove dead _maybe_wrap_cuda_graph def + 6 identity calls. KEY REFINEMENT vs v1: Edit 2.9b rewritten as 6 unique exact-match OLD->NEW blocks (v1 hand-waved 'apply by line number bottom-up' for the 5 shared sites) — verified the line two-above each call differs at every site, so a 3-line OLD block is globally unique; order-independent. Confirmed dead-code KEEPs: MambaModel/SelectiveSSMLayer are LIVE (tests/hw/test_mamba_megakernel.py:37-39 does `import grokking_race_v2 as g; g.MambaModel(...)`; mamba_oracle.py/mamba3_oracle.py transcribe SelectiveSSMLayer), and _maybe_checkpoint is live in all three model forwards — only _maybe_wrap_cuda_graph removed. Verified evaluate()